[[File:Silver Gull mouth.jpg|thumb|right|A Silver Gull squawking]]
==English==

===Pronunciation===
*{{IPA|/skwɔːk/}}
*{{audio|en-us-squawk.ogg|Audio (US)}}
*{{rhymes|ɔːk}}
*homophone: ''[[squark]]'' in non-rhotic dialects

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[shrill]] [[noise]], especially made by a [[voice]] or [[bird]]; a [[yell]], [[scream]], [[call]], or shunpo.
# {{aviation}} A four-digit transponder code used by aircraft for identification or transmission of emergency signals.
# {{aviation}} An issue or complaint related to aircraft maintenance.
# The [[American night heron]].

====Translations====
{{trans-top|shrill noise}}
{{trans-mid}}
* Spanish: {{t|es|graznido|m}}, {{t|es|chillido|m}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To make a squawking noise; to yell, scream, or call out shrilly.
# To [[speak]] [[out]]; to [[protest]].
# To [[report]] an [[infraction]]; to [[rat]] on or [[tattle]]; to [[disclose]] a [[secret]].
# {{aviation}} To set or transmit a four-digit transponder code. {{non-gloss definition|(Normally followed by the specific code in question.)}}

